---
/*
 * "Report a problem" and "For coding agents" (`llms.txt`), under every page,
 * laid out as the next/previous links under them are: at either edge, each
 * label after a line icon of the arrows' size, so the labels line up.
 *
 * There's no "Edit page" link while the repository doesn't take outside
 * contributions; "Improve this page with your coding agent" replaces it once
 * it does.
 *
 * `llms.txt` lists every page's Markdown version, for an agent to read.
 *
 * Search leaves the row out: it's the same on every page.
 */
import { Icon } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';

const REPOSITORY = 'https://github.com/kindgi/kindgi-sdk';

const route = Astro.locals.starlightRoute;

const page = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, 'https://docs.kindgi.com').href;
const issue = new URL(`${REPOSITORY}/issues/new`);
issue.searchParams.set('title', `Docs: ${route.entry.data.title}`);
issue.searchParams.set('body', `Page: ${page}\n\nWhat's wrong or missing:\n`);

const llms = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/')}llms.txt`;
---

<div class="kindgi-page-links sl-flex print:hidden" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <a href={issue.href} class="sl-flex">
    <Icon name="comment-alt" size="1rem" />
    Report a problem
  </a>
  <a href={llms} class="sl-flex">
    <Icon name="list-format" size="1rem" />
    For coding agents
  </a>
</div>

<style>
  .kindgi-page-links {
    flex-grow: 1;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  a {
    gap: 0.375rem;
    align-items: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }
  a:hover {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
</style>
